    "https://www.rockford.edu/community/humanresources/studentopenings/": {
      "title": "Student Employment Opportunities",
      "description": "Student Employment Opportunities » Rockford University Apply Now Contact Us Contact Us About Newsroom Give Library my.rockford.edu Search Mobile Navigation Academics PROGRAMS Academics Colleges and Deans Majors and Minors Undergraduate Degrees Academic Departments Professional & Extended Learning RU Online Graduate Programs Puri School of Business English Language Institute (ESL) Study Abroad Early Scholars Student Support Programming RESOURCES & SUPPORT Library Academic Affairs and Provost Academic Integrity Policy Registrar Transcript Request The HUB: Academic Coaching & Testing Services Catalog and Resources Calendars and Schedules Writing Center Spirit Shop Online Bookstore ROCKFORD DIFFERENCE Why Rockford University Community-Based Learning Phi Beta Kappa (PBK) Learning Expectations Accreditations Admission INFORMATION FOR First Year Undergraduate Transfer International Student Admitted Undergraduate RU Online Graduate Programs TUITION & FINANCIAL AID Rockford Promise Financial Aid and Scholarships Financial Aid: Step by Step Guide Tuition and Fees First-Year Student Calculator Transfer Student Calculator CONNECT Request More Information Visit and Tour Campus Apply to Rockford University Campus & Community FOR STUDENTS Campus & Community Career Development Commencement First-Year Experience Residence Life Student Activities Student Administrative Services Student Success Student Life CAMPUS SERVICES Campus Map Spirit Shop Box Office Business Office Dining Services Disability Services IT: Information Technology Marketing & Communications Lang Wellness Center Dept of Public Safety Scheduling Services and Rentals Community President’s Office About Rockford University Calendar of Events Compliance and Title IX Global Affairs Human Resources and Employment Jane Addams Center See Something Say Something Behavioral Alert Business Summit Arts & Lectures LOCATIONS & RESOURCES Art Gallery Box Office Theatres EVENTS & PERFORMANCES Arts & Lectures Forum Series Music Ensembles Performing Arts Season Athletics MEN’S SPORTS Baseball Basketball Cross Country Football Soccer Volleyball WOMEN’S SPORTS Basketball Cross Country Golf Soccer Softball Volleyball Flag Football Bowling RESOURCES & FAN ZONE Rockford Regents Alumni STAY IN TOUCH Alumni Alumni Association Contact Us Alumni Awards Transcript & Diploma Request ENGAGE Catalyst FOPA WRCR Golf Playday Day of Giving Homecoming Weekend Charles M. DeWild Hall Of Fame GIVE BACK Gala Alumni Referral Scholarship The Annual Fund Legacy Giving Ways to Give Student Employment Opportunities Rockford.edu / Campus & Community / Human Resources / Student Employment Opportunities Student Employment Opportunities Many full-time, undergraduate students qualify for Student Employment while attending Rockford University. If you are interested in working, please review this information so you are prepared when you arrive. Please note that you must bring original forms of identification with you to campus so as not to delay your start date. Open Positions Apply for a position by filling out the Student Employment Application. In order for your application to be processed, students MUST use their Rockford University email address.  (@rockford.edu).  The application will not go through if you use an outside email. Position: CBS Lab Assistant/Tutor Supervisor: Deb Breiter- DBreiter@rockford.edu CBS Lab Assistant The Lab Assistant will support the Chemical and Biological Sciences (CBS) Department by preparing laboratory materials, assisting in the setup and breakdown of lab experiments, and ensuring a clean and safe laboratory environment. The ideal candidate will have a background in biology and/or chemistry, attention to detail, and the ability to follow instructions accurately. Qualifications:  Successful completion of BIOL 150/151 or equivalent or CHEM 105/106 or equivalent. CBS Tutor The Tutor will provide academic support to students enrolled in biology and/or chemistry courses. They will help students understand complex concepts, improve their study and problem-solving skills, and prepare for exams. Qualifications: Successful completion of equivalent courses and a strong background in biology and/or chemistry, excellent communication skills, and an interest in helping students succeed. Position: Football Assistant Supervisor: Calvin Toliver- Ctoliver@rockford.edu There are 3 different positions available for Football.  They include a team manager, filmer and Laundry Washer. There are several other departments on campus that have open positions throughout the academic year that include: Athletics Library Admissions English Department Box Office SAS Advancement Performing Arts IT Spirt Shop Student Government Student Life You can reach out to the individual departments to see if they have or will have any open positions. Work Authorization Form To qualify for student employment, you must accept Campus Employment or Federal Work Study as part of your financial aid package. Accepting one of these options will result in a Work Authorization Form. You must get a Work Authorization Card from Student Administrative Services (1st floor, Nelson Hall or by emailing SAS ) prior to interviewing. A work authorization form must be provided to each supervisor at the time of your interview or when filling out the student employment application. Complete Employment Paperwork at Human Resources You will not be able to start working until you have completed necessary paperwork at Human Resources (1st floor, Puri School of Business). You will receive an email to schedule an orientation once HR has been notified that you have been hired. You must bring original forms of identification to the orientation for the Federal I-9 form (Most common are a photo ID, Social Security Card, Certified copy of your birth certificate and Passport). No photocopies/faxes/scanned documents will be accepted. All International Students must bring their Visa and any other related documents. Direct Deposit is the preferred method of payment. Ensure you bring your routing and account number. Section Menu Faculty Employment Opportunities Graduate Assistant Employment Opportunities Staff Employment Opportunities Student Employment Opportunities Human Resources PURI School of Business, Lower Level 5050 E. State Street Rockford, IL 61108 815-394-5026 fax: 815.226.4190 Sedasia Washington, Sr. HR Generalist swashington@rockford.edu Hours: Mon-Fri - 8:30 am to 5:00 pm ROCKFORD UNIVERSITY 5050 East State Street Rockford IL 61108 815.226.4000 Faculty & Staff Directory Campus Map & Directions Virtual Tour - Visit Campus Today Library Majors and Minors my.rockford.edu Online Interactive Academic Catalog Employment Opportunities Lang Wellness Center Compliance and Title IX Emergency Information Give News Event Calendar About Rockford University President’s Office Privacy Policy IBHE Feedback Scheduling Services and Rentals Copyright © 2026 Rockford University, all rights reserved"
    },
